      "hutton_perspective": "Hutton notes the paradox that Calvin's Geneva, often presented as a model of ordered godly discipline, nonetheless prosecuted witches, illustrating that Protestant reformation did not inherently reduce witch prosecution and might intensify the theological anxiety that drove it.",
      "ginzburg_perspective": "The Geneva 'greasers' cases of 1545 are an unusual variant of the witch trial—focused on plague-spreading rather than the standard sabbath template—that raises questions about the multiple forms that diabolism accusations could take in response to different social anxieties."
