      "clark_perspective": "Clark reads James VI's Daemonologie as a serious intellectual contribution to demonological literature, noting that the king engaged with and responded to sceptical arguments (particularly Reginald Scot's Discoverie of Witchcraft) with theological and philosophical sophistication, placing the North Berwick case within a tradition of learned Protestant demonology.",
