      "hutton_perspective": "Hutton emphasizes that the accused Demdike and Chattox families were practitioners of cunning craft—healing, charming, curse-lifting—whose activities placed them in a culturally ambiguous position exploited by prosecution. The rivalry between families was a social precondition for the cascade of accusations.",
