      "clark_perspective": "Clark analyses Binsfeld's Tractatus as a serious contribution to demonological theory defending torture-extracted confessions as valid on the grounds that diabolical assistance could not long withstand proper inquisitorial procedure, illustrating the coherent theological logic underpinning prosecution.",
      "hutton_perspective": "Hutton frames Trier as an instance of extreme official-driven persecution where learned elite anxiety about diabolical conspiracy, amplified by a decade of poor harvests and political insecurity, drove prosecution far beyond any organic community accusation.",
