      "hutton_perspective": "Hutton notes the paradox that the Spanish Inquisition, often regarded as the most feared tribunal in Europe, was in fact more sceptical about witchcraft claims than many secular courts, and that Salazar's investigation represents the most rigorous application of evidential standards to witch trial claims in the early modern period.",
